{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,5,14]],"date-time":"2026-05-14T14:26:58Z","timestamp":1778768818996,"version":"3.51.4"},"reference-count":8,"publisher":"World Scientific Pub Co Pte Lt","issue":"08","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["Int. J. Mod. Phys. D"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2005,8]]},"abstract":"<jats:p> The construction of a radar coordinate system about the world line of an observer is discussed. Radar coordinates for a hyperbolic observer as well as a uniformly rotating observer are described in detail. The utility of the notion of radar distance and the admissibility of radar coordinates are investigated. Our results provide a critical assessment of the physical significance of radar coordinates. </jats:p>","DOI":"10.1142/s0218271805006961","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2005,8,24]],"date-time":"2005-08-24T05:41:52Z","timestamp":1124862112000},"page":"1413-1429","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":15,"title":["LIMITATIONS OF RADAR COORDINATES"],"prefix":"10.1142","volume":"14","author":[{"given":"DONATO","family":"BINI","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Istituto per le Applicazioni del Calcolo \"M. Picone\", CNR I-00161 Rome, Italy"},{"name":"International Center for Relativistic Astrophysics — I.C.R.A., University of Rome \"La Sapienza\", I-00185 Rome, Italy"},{"name":"INFN Sezione di Firenze, via G. Sansone, 1, I-50019 Sesto Fiorentino (FI), Italy"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"LUCA","family":"LUSANNA","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"INFN Sezione di Firenze, via G. Sansone, 1, I-50019 Sesto Fiorentino (FI), Italy"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"BAHRAM","family":"MASHHOON","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Physics and Astronomy, University of Missouri-Columbia, Columbia, Missou